From 84c505b834797c4f160c583f8a4fe9f70ab27a05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gugu-acp <gugu-acp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:16:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] gugu: serve _session/steering on ACP v2, into any
 foreground work

Why: Gugu injects a message that arrives while the agent works (a group
message, a "send now" from the queue) with `_session/steering`, delivered at
the next tool boundary (0001). The v2 surface did not serve the method and
filtered it out of the v2 `initialize`, so a v2 client could only queue a
second prompt behind the running work.

- The v2 surface serves `_session/steering` and advertises it in the top-level
  `_meta`, as v1 does. A v2 client has no legacy contract to keep: a steer
  while no work runs returns `promptRequired`, and the client sends the
  message as a prompt (whose echo hands off a turn held for background
  subagents).
- steer() injects while the session has foreground work, not only while a
  Turn is unsettled: a model cycle that Claude Code started on its own (its
  follow-up after a background task) is the session's work too. Such a cycle
  has no Turn, so the steer needs no marks; the cycle's result names the
  message and ends the work as for any cycle. This replaces the second half
  of the old 0006, which read Claude Code's global session state instead;
  v2 reports the foreground work itself, so 0006 is dropped.

Upstream: none yet; extends the steering contract (agentclientprotocol/
claude-agent-acp#1175 for `delivery: "next"`) to the v2 surface.

Drop when: upstream serves steering on v2, with steering into a cycle that
Claude Code started on its own.
